            <ArticleTitle>[Direct thrombin antagonists].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Inhibiting thrombin as a key enzyme of the coagulation cascade is therapeutically useful in thromboembolic diseases. In coronary thrombosis, direct thrombin inhibitors promise to be useful for an efficacious therapy. Hirudin and recombinant or synthetic mimetics like hirulog, argatroban and melagatran have proven their efficacy in clinical studies.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Therapy with direct thrombin inhibitors such as hirudin and analogous substances reduces coronary events. Moreover, the agents are useful for therapy of thromboembolic diseases, especially in the case of heparin induced thrombocytopenia type II.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
